gate cannot become one by construction.\n\nSECOND LIMIT, AS LOUD AS THE FIRST. A path outside `akasha/` is judged by no check even on this road, which `akasha write --help` states outright. Most of this migration ablates files outside `akasha/`, so most of it stays unjudged either way.\n\nTHIRD LIMIT, FOUND WHILE LANDING THIS. A change near the root of the import graph inherits every type error already there in its closure. Landing this module into `command-system` was refused with 153 diagnostics across 31 files it does not touch, among them `alan/fitness/commands/*` and `infrastructure/inference-commands/*`. It had to land through the glass at 5d76216c65. The checked road is therefore usable at the leaves and unusable near the root while the folder is not green.\n\nCOST. Fixed cost per batch dominates: one file 15.7 to 18.2 seconds over five samples, 100 orphan files in one batch 19.4 seconds, a 100-file importer closure 18.2 seconds refused with one TS2307 per importer. Mechanical baseline for 101 files was 2.24 seconds. So roughly 16 seconds fixed per batch and 30 milliseconds per file: at 200 files a batch, a 1,000-file migration costs about 80 seconds of checking against 10 mechanical. Affordable as a default on cost alone.",
